    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116044" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ωγενος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠκεανός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				231
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i>, etc.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠγηνός</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Pherecyd.
			</span></i> Syr.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				2
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠγήν</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆνος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠγενίδαι</span></b> 
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠκεανίδαι</span>
			, Id.; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠγένιος</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχαῖος, ὠ. Στυγὸς
				ὕδωρ</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Parth.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				7
			</span></i>. cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠγένιον: παλαιόν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
